# AGENTS.md ({name})

This file holds **the map of this repository**, **where it differs from what Rotproof keeps**, and **short rules that
apply to every change**. The rules Rotproof keeps (the layers, the records, how to run `rotproof check`) are in
`.rotproof/AGENTS.md`: read it too.

## Map

| Path | Content |
|---|---|
{map}| `docs/` | Records, as one OKF 0.2 bundle: specs and work items (`docs/work/`, open and closed), knowledge (`docs/knowledge/`: how things are now, and why), log (`docs/log.md`) |
| `.config/rotproof.toml` | The structure this project declares for Rotproof |
| `.rotproof/` | Rotproof's own files, rewritten by `rotproof create`. Never edited by hand |

## Differences from what Rotproof keeps

- None (as made by `rotproof create`). Write here when a layer is removed or an entry point follows a framework's
  convention. A difference that is not written here looks like a mistake to the next reader.

## Rules for every change

- **Run `rotproof check` before handing over a change.** It is what CI runs.
- **After adding a check, plant the forbidden form and confirm the check fails, and read why it failed.**
